l  ingredients in Chinese cooking in my  and almost everything extra fry  everything begins with ginger and garlic  so we're gonna have five sizes of ginger  and six cloves of garlic I'm gonna toss  that into the oil and we're gonna stir  fry that saute it and really sweat the  flavors out and infused into the oil  we're gonna add one tablespoon of sugar  and we're gonna melt the sugar into the  oil next we're gonna be adding the  liquids to the wok and this will be the  beginning of our braising liquid so  we're looking at light soy sauce dark  soy sauce and Chinese rice wine these  three will be the foundation of the  coloring and the flavor of the sauce  Chinese rice wine has a very floral  essence to it the way it smells the way  it tastes and we'll need about 1/2 a cup  of Chinese rice wine after that add a  quarter cup of light soy sauce and after  that add one and a half tablespoons of  dark soy sauce and that's gonna give  thick the hue the color of this dish to  balance out the savoriness and the sweet  in the floral miss we're also going to  add three tablespoons of vinegar just  regular vinegar adding just a slight  amount of tang to it and now we're gonna  start introducing our dry ingredients  our herbs in this bowl I got some star  anis some cloves and some bay leaves now  the star needs I have it is near the  bottom of the bag and so I have all the  broken pieces now pretty sure it grabbed  about three star aneesa's worth of star  anis crumbs in this mix I also have six  cloves and three bay leaves we're gonna  plop all that stuff in there mix it  around and it's in the starch mode real  good every time a cuckoo star nice Isaac  over  I'm making fun at home because he loves  but and Star News is a big part of the  Fabri it's like that unique cinnamon  flavor so because of the star news I  know Isaac will like this dish too  alright so now that we got all our  ingredients mixed in you might be  wondering well this is a really salt and  dish there's a lot of soy sauce in there  while you're right it's gonna be very  salty if you don't add some water to it  so it's very strong flavors at this  point we're gonna tame that flavor a  little bit with some water and we're  gonna add about 3 cups of water and this  would also raise the braising liquid sup  high enough so that we can submerge our  bird we bring up the braising liquid to  a boil and we carefully lower the bird  back into the wok now it's a full wok  full of boiling liquids so be careful  don't just pop it in there I've done  that before and it's not very fun now I  always like to put the breast side down  first because it's the thickest portion  of the duck in terms of needing to cook  through the duck so I put the breast  side down first and turn the heat down  to low and let it simmer now you want to  cook this dish for a total about 45 to  50 minutes that works out to about 2 to  3 flips every 15 minutes so after every  15 minutes we're gonna go back we're  gonna flip it and we're gonna expose the  back of the duck to the braising liquids  breast side up and after another 15  minutes of that flip back around breast  side down again I'm just back and forth  up until about the 4550 minute mark and  this already depends on the size of your  duck I guess if you have a huge-mongous  dog maybe even go for a full hour all  right so now the duck is done with the  braising process we're gonna go ahead  and set up that baking dish that we had  earlier with the duck we're gonna put a  rack inside the baking dish so we can't  elevate the duck from being sitting in  its own juices now it's time to work on  the glaze  now the glaze is it's very simple  nothing fancy it's literally one part  honey one part water one tablespoon of  water  microwave it get it to be hot and then I  like to add my tablespoon of honey and  then because of the heat of the water  obviously the honey is gonna melt easily  into the water mix it up whisk it  together and voila you got your honey  glaze very very simple stuff and what  we're gonna do with this honey glaze is  gonna we're gonna just  on top of the skin so then we can have  some sugar on the outside of the skin  someone would kindly do the last part  which is roasting the duck the sugar in  the honey will help char the skin which  then creates a nice outside texture for  the skin and it's gonna be you  and once the duck is done being glazed  we are going to put it in the oven the  oven should be set at 425 degrees  Fahrenheit we want it relatively high so  a catch are the skin of the duck and  we're gonna roast it for about 15 to 20  minutes or until the skin is crispy to  your liking and once you're done  crisping the skin go ahead and pull it  out and let the duck rest for 10 minutes  and let all the juices redistribute into  the muscles and into the meat of the  duck and the next part is the best part  serving time now you can always serve  this as with some rice or inside of  noodles generally I like to put this  with rice but sometimes I just like the  caveman it too and just eat it as is all  right moment of truth guys duck sauce  [Music]  conversion and duck is hugely underrated  in my opinion no one ever talks about  duck holiday seasons it's always turkey  I'm tell you though duck is where it's  at it is a fan of your bird but because  of the fat it's also a juicier bird this  is a nice nostalgic meal right here  the aroma in my kitchen the flavors in  my mouth it was part of my childhood  right here yeah I hope you guys enjoyed  this cooking video I if you never had  duck before again give it a try let me  know what you think I'm gonna start  making these cooking videos more often  again I really haven't been doing a good  job with making cooking videos on the  regular but moving forward into the new  year I'm gonna try and make more cooking  videos and feel free to let me know what  you want to see me make and I look  forward to seeing your comments down  below  [Music]  [Music]

